Paper presentation round 1: new title, Figure 1 redrawn, appendix rewritten without the log, tables centred

- Title: "MemShift: Noticing a Change Is Not Repairing It in LLM-Derived Personal Memory".
- Figure 1 redrawn in TikZ with icons (fontawesome5): what changes, what an item stores (B, D), what
  each part governs, and the two headline results.
- memtab ends its paragraph, so side tables are centred (old Tables 34 and 44); appendix floats stay
  inside their section and may sit here, at the top, at the bottom or on a float page.
- Appendix rewritten in five parts (app_a..app_e) without process narrative: 56 to 27 pages;
  dropped generated tables that repeated others (per-contrast control intervals, decomposition,
  writer predictors, test sensitivity, robustness duplicates, native per-system table, membership
  subset); appendix_stage4.tex replaced by app_d.tex.
- Main text polished for density and one name per mechanism (the authored derivation's former name
  "extractor" kept until round 2); bibliography set small.
- Generators: native-null table may take a float page and has a shorter caption; neighbour caption
  points to the released audit record; class-split figure axis no longer clips the orphan branch.

